{# The theme's hero, with the picture written into the page instead of linked.

   The theme links every picture, and a linked drawing renders in a document of
   its own: the tokens in it fall back to their light values and a frame is
   drawn around it, whatever mode the reader is in. The picture here is a
   drawing in Soul's own diagram grammar, and inline it reads the page's tokens
   -- so it follows the reader into dark, and stands on the canvas with no
   frame, as decoration beside the claim rather than a figure to open.

   Everything else is the theme's template as it stands. #}
<div class="sds-sections">
    <div class="sds-split sds-split--center">
        <div class="sds-column">
            {{- renderNode(node.children|first) -}}
        </div>
        <div class="sds-column">
            {{ source(node.option('src')) }}
        </div>
    </div>
    {%- for child in node.children|slice(1) -%}
        {{ renderNode(child) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
</div>
